{
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "tool",
      "name": "quote",
      "output_key": "quote",
      "tool": "market_quote",
      "args": {
        "ticker": "{{question}}"
      },
      "fail_ok": true
    },
    {
      "type": "tool",
      "name": "path",
      "output_key": "path",
      "tool": "candlesticks",
      "args": {
        "ticker": "{{question}}",
        "hours_back": 0.75,
        "hourly": false
      },
      "fail_ok": true
    },
    {
      "type": "tool",
      "name": "tape",
      "output_key": "tape",
      "tool": "previous_trades",
      "args": {
        "ticker": "{{question}}",
        "limit": 20
      },
      "fail_ok": true
    },
    {
      "type": "prompt",
      "name": "analyze_context",
      "output_key": "context",
      "prompt": "Game: {{game}}\nRecent minute bars: {{path}}\n\nAnalyze:\n1. Time remaining: what minute is it, how many minutes left (90min match, account for period)\n2. Recent price momentum: compare last 3-5 minute bars - is price trending up, down, or stable?\n3. Goal timing: when was the most recent goal (check game events and candlestick spikes)? Has it been >5 min since a goal (absorbed) or <3 min (still spiking)?\n4. Score situation: who's winning, and does time decay favor them or opponent?\n\nBe specific with numbers and timing.",
      "tools": [],
      "max_tool_iterations": 0,
      "output_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "minutes_remaining": {
            "type": "number",
            "description": "Approximate minutes left in match"
          },
          "recent_trend": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": ["rising", "falling", "stable", "post_spike_drift"],
            "description": "Price momentum from last few minute bars"
          },
          "minutes_since_last_goal": {
            "type": "number",
            "description": "Minutes since most recent goal, or 999 if no recent goal"
          },
          "time_decay_direction": {
            "type": "string",
            "enum": ["up", "down", "neutral"],
            "description": "Does running clock favor this outcome (up) or opponent (down) or neutral"
          },
          "reasoning": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Brief explanation of the analysis"
          }
        },
        "required": ["minutes_remaining", "recent_trend", "minutes_since_last_goal", "time_decay_direction", "reasoning"],
        "additionalProperties": false
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "prompt",
      "name": "predict",
      "output_key": "prediction",
      "prompt": "Contract: {{question}}\nCurrent book: {{quote}}\nGame state: {{game}}\nRecent prints: {{tape}}\nContext analysis: {{context}}\n\nForecast the 5-minute price move. Key patterns to consider:\n\n1. TIME DECAY (most reliable): If <20 minutes remain and one team leads, the trailing team's price decays -1 to -3c per 5min. The leading team's price rises +1 to +3c per 5min. This is continuous and predictable.\n\n2. POST-GOAL MEAN REVERSION: If a goal was scored <3 minutes ago (check spike in candlesticks), the price likely spiked and will drift back -1 to -2c as the book digests.\n\n3. MOMENTUM CONTINUATION: If price has been trending consistently for 5+ minutes, it may continue another +1 to -1c unless there's a clear reason to reverse.\n\n4. STALE BOOK DRIFT: On very thin books (small recent volume), a single large order may have moved the mid artificially; it drifts back -1 to +1c.\n\n5. QUIET PERIODS: If none of the above apply (early in match, stable score, no recent action), predict 0.\n\nBe willing to predict non-zero moves when patterns are clear. Time decay in final 20 minutes is especially reliable. Quote tighter spreads (1-2c half-width) when confident in the pattern, wider (3-4c) when uncertain.\n\nYour forecast is the CHANGE in cents, not the absolute price. Negative for down, positive for up.",
      "tools": [],
      "max_tool_iterations": 0,
      "output_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "delta_cents": {
            "type": "number",
            "description": "How many cents the mid will MOVE over the next five minutes. Negative for down, 0 for no move. Do not state a price — state the change."
          },
          "half_width_cents": {
            "type": "number",
            "description": "Half the width of the tightest two-sided market you would actually stand behind, in cents. Narrow (1-2c) when pattern is clear, wide (3-4c) when uncertain."
          },
          "confidence": {
            "type": "number",
            "description": "0-1. How sure, given how thin and noisy this book is."
          },
          "driver": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The one thing you expect to move it, or why nothing will. Name the specific pattern."
          },
          "falsifier": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "What would show this call was wrong, before settlement."
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "delta_cents",
          "half_width_cents",
          "confidence",
          "driver",
          "falsifier"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false
      }
    }
  ]
}

